&lt;h2 id="garden-description">Garden Description&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>A grove and shrine of Apollo in the mountaintop town of Kyrtones in Boeotia was visited by Pausanias in the 2nd century CE &lt;a href="http://data.perseus.org/citations/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0525.tlg001.perseus-eng1:9.24.4">(9.24.4)&lt;/a>. There was also a natural spring at the site, next to which was a sanctuary of the Nymphs and a small grove of fruit-bearing trees.&lt;/p>
